---
title: "sale lifecycle (LegionPreLiquidApprovedSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: initialize(params)
    q_init --> q_active: Sale is active, investors can invest
    q_active --> q_ended: end() by LegionOrProject
    q_active --> q_canceled: cancel() by Project (whenTokensNotSupplied)
    q_ended --> q_refundWindow: Refund period starts
    q_refundWindow --> q_refundOver: block.timestamp >= endTime + refundDuration
    q_refundOver --> q_publishCapital: publishRaisedCapital(capitalRaised) by Legion
    q_publishCapital --> q_publishTge: publishTgeDetails(askToken, tokenPrice, decimals) by Legion
    q_publishTge --> q_supplyTokens: supplyTokens(amount, legionFee, referrerFee) by Project
    q_supplyTokens --> q_claimable: Investors can claimTokenAllocation
    q_claimable --> q_withdrawCapital: withdrawRaisedCapital() by Project
    q_withdrawCapital --> [*]: Capital distributed minus fees
    q_canceled --> q_refundCancel: withdrawInvestedCapitalIfCanceled() by investors
    q_refundCancel --> [*]: All capital returned

    note right of q_active
        INV-001: Sale cannot be canceled after tokens are supplied
        INV-002: invest() requires valid unused signature
    end note

    note right of q_refundWindow
        INV-003: Refund period must elapse before any capital withdrawal
        INV-004: publishRaisedCapital requires refund period over
    end note

    note right of q_supplyTokens
        INV-005: Token supply must match expected allocation + fees
        INV-006: Tokens supplied only once (whenTokensNotSupplied guard)
    end note
